{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Dan, a lion's whelp.</b> That he would stand at the border and lie in wait and guard over Israel lest enemies enter the land." "<b>He shall leap from the Bashan.</b> That he drinks the waters of the Jordan, which cascade from the Bashan, for the Jordan emerges from the cave of Paneas, which is in the land of Dan — and therefore its name is called Jordan, יורד דן. And it separates between the land of the Bashan, which is the land of Og, and the bank of the Jordan, which belonged to the side of the land of Israel. And the land that borders the Jordan is very good, as it is said: ״ויבחר לו לוט את כל ככר הירדן כי כלה משקה״ etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:03.178266274Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}